ons With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050240 #edb/ref 1033 493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050240 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "38bc1722-543b-58cb-b448-fb93b0e623de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186161968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1031 "Creating Rows or Columns Containing Zeros Using Gaussian Elimination" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1033 3029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1034 0.2853007808149399 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "508ac00e-0867-53e8-a192-d981ff4bbdc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1031 "Systems of Equations as Augmented Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1033 148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1034 0.6027738609637455 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "64dbabd7-08e6-5435-b006-ab4997312f47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186104027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186104028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186104029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186104030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186104031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104026 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a117e6ad-ea85-5ffa-be6d-c20de27fa2cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104027 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨1 - 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104027 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104027 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b9f1382a-870c-5f7c-b007-6684dc65136e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104028 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104028 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104028 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e68d6a57-2fff-5fe1-97e2-53e0d4e0fb15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104029 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨1,-2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104029 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104029 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee0db42e-1100-5418-8315-c630442bb8ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104030 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨ - 1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104030 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104030 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56c35cf2-8374-5cfd-8ca3-d7861125849e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104031 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨1, 0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104031 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186104031 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7ec12860-5f4a-5e06-8d80-fe18641609f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105602 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105602 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](images/97/9773630254747a4bbd072bd44a6263bdd078fa09005b1bb5f51c48b894d67daf.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105602 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7bfabbd2-9988-5c0e-9c17-3d430b3e7a0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105602 #edb/ref 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n![](images/43/43b9b089e0f93e63acf386bb605a0e3751cc8660899ce19d23835f9f79918bcc.svg)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n![](images/4a/4a598a80f2f14715d1f10d182b3f80887c7586beabecc2a329119b624c19a4fa.svg)\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105603 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105603 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/bc/bcbd79c8cac28ef6bb4dc07a04789692d9726df238b4907841825244432c5783.svg)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105603 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "681fce57-6be7-5907-b575-8c34b4819ae5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105603 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n![](images/d3/d381e04f0a7eb2973e20c9f397ef2e2267f90ac6992cfacd3a8927b4d48138a9.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/89/89ca081f99d8cbd33bb11e58ef6aa91aa3045a02ff06c9877a53b9e2f88874db.svg)\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186402782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1039 "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186551473 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105745 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186561382 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105746 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving 2x2 Singular Systems of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106000 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0211c399-b12f-5dd5-8ac4-97409f9a60bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186104026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186379835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0407db63-d38b-50cb-b37f-dfd7ce1a8b10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106313 #edb/ref 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186106635 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106635 #edb/ref 1061 17192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b66da6f-e7b3-547c-b47a-3bfe17bbc205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106636 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106636 #edb/ref 1061 17193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106636 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "414f018d-78f3-5c78-86b8-6363d86d3a9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106636 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106637 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106637 #edb/ref 1061 17194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106637 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00d5123d-64a7-5878-9b67-ac7b7a2bf0a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106637 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106638 #edb/ref 1061 17195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106638 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dc00947a-2ca5-59a7-a7a8-349b27d59bf2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106638 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106744 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106744 #edb/ref 1061 23052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106744 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e6eff47b-880f-55d6-94ac-af8b9767c4fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106744 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107080 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/6a/6a69daf7712312876b0ec97c540bbc472e46a7938beb8a59e694a04ad0b1d8c6.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/a8/a8bfe3f6b27247ee9b27db8346fd94fb9068c85dec6f4a71517a821dee48dbf3.svg)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 2y = -5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we describe the **general solution** of our system.\n\n- The first variable in our equation, $x,$ is called a **basic variable**.\n\n- The second variable in our equation, $y,$ is called a **free variable**.\n\nSolving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x = -5+2y.$ So the general solution of the system is\n![](images/0b/0ba4a232f29dd6fce2a8f6d7cda39b4f5b192c20fc91fe4403dfe648231382c5.svg)\nwhere the free variable $y$ is any number.\n\nIn vector form, this solution is written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this is the equation of a straight line on a plane. Any point on this line satisfies our system of equations.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $y$ and find the corresponding value of $x$ on the line. For example, if we choose $y=0,$ then the corresponding value is $x=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-5,$ $y=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186107080 #edb/ref 1065 3153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107080 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0c91df0b-40c7-5a65-9fda-5d2d6438dfa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107080 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107081 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a $2 \\times 2$ system of linear equations, we have the following possibilities for the number of solutions:\n\n- The system has exactly *one solution* if and only if the respective coefficient matrix is non-singular (meaning that the determinant is not zero). Such systems are called **consistent independent**.\n\n- The system has *infinitely many solutions* if the second row in the standard echelon form contains only $0$'s. These systems are called **consistent dependent**.\n\n- The system has *no solution* if the second row in the standard echelon form contains only $0$'s on the left-hand side and a non-zero element on the right-hand side. These are called **inconsistent** systems.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\n**Note:** A system of linear equations of the form \n![](images/cb/cb397dd01794f28ff11c01079e287d63175e439c8bbaa85cd02dc61689780fa8.svg)\nwhere we have only $0$'s on the right-hand side, is called **homogeneous**. A homogeneous system always has at least one solution, namely, the solution $x=0$ and $y=0.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle 0,0 \\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107081 #edb/ref 1065 3154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107081 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b885f832-9e76-5008-a764-7375b1c25e35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107081 #edb/ref 1067 "The Number of Solutions of a 2x2 System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107097 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, a system of equations might not have any solutions. For example, consider the following augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is\n![](images/e8/e8c64d8be247afd3e8ab02abc69e33635ef0234dbcbbc60f42379021a39a58a2.svg)\n\nThe final equation, $0x+0y=10,$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=10,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186107097 #edb/ref 1065 3901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107097 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "20c281f5-a455-581a-a7f7-fec6cfaa114e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107097 #edb/ref 1067 "Singular Systems with No Solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263037 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186263037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04406210-94a5-519d-b563-c1787d94b573" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263293 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186263293 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263293 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20136c69-8c25-5eeb-a342-b87289d36eda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263386 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263386 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263386 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2dd5fd9e-9a95-5bbe-b9ca-15b27ae75731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264011 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186264011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "742c670e-1f11-5451-982a-0b676be9c761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264517 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186264517 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264517 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b006db61-2f57-5349-bc2a-2f6efb0cae8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186263386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265366 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3ff41cad-65a8-5c50-a758-f7388a3a1397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ -4x+8y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df63ef93-068d-5156-97ea-60671ff0c81c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266012 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186285449 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186285449 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285449 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47c97c9a-b257-58e1-b8f0-fedf81973715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285709 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186285709 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285709 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6572eab8-0051-57e0-9e01-2a886e1ff7f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285962 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186285962 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285962 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7fb0f231-ef58-570a-a217-3ac725a9c673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286302 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a610291f-fe71-59f4-ba82-34c306fd05eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286824 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186286824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "df55ab77-72af-5c93-956c-d075379dc2c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186285709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287354 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "613521d7-e573-530c-9e5e-83c95de64ea2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 2x+8y &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9e4d803-6c25-5024-8fca-536e9832cf45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288009 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327089 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327089 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327089 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "124cd317-220b-5b1b-b0df-11ccb5699d8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327411 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327411 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327411 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36c238b2-e923-54d5-9366-3b0928bcfd68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327452 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6-9y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327452 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327452 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b279e3a-1875-5863-9a8a-f83033667b33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327597 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327597 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327597 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c3ca48a-486f-5497-9863-4452db258c31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327825 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186327825 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327825 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66bc3170-2988-5341-bdeb-88dc944a6924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186327411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329466 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a49ef358-bb1d-5f86-95ec-c04c91c0bf60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=4 \\\\ 6x+42y &=24.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2bf7b16f-c404-5080-a0f3-019c76bbad3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329635 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & -24\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 42 & 24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=4 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+7y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4-7y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-7y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-7y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186339610 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339610 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339610 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "35e6a7c5-5218-5d25-a8f6-7848a5bca3fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339713 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186339713 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339713 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42fb3843-e811-598c-9cd8-40fa0350bea1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339928 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186339928 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339928 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57cf24ad-e2ac-533d-8f71-64d4e595fa8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340708 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186340708 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340708 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad94e501-a2d3-5422-a57f-c8541c6ecb28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340992 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186340992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340992 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d21c64f6-9851-5d4c-8362-9495bc2b9f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339713 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186339610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341690 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0dcd427-5fab-5d80-85bc-c5c9b1007acd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342079 #edb/ref 1069 "q